<title>FRANCE: MATIF financial futures volume up 21 pct in Sept.</title>
<headline>MATIF financial futures volume up 21 pct in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of financial futures and options contracts traded on the French MATIF exchange in September rose 21.0 percent from August but fell 17.8 percent from September 1995, Matif said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for financial contracts were as follows:</p>
<p>			   Volume     Change    Change  Open positions</p>
<p>					 on month   on year  at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	6.11 bln  +21.0 pct   -17.8 pct   974,554</p>
<p>  Financial futures 5.13 bln  +21.0 pct   -15.8 pct   492,262</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond 3.31 bln  +54.8 pct   -11.0 pct   230,244</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	 1.27 bln  -25.3 pct   -23.8 pct   194,286</p>
<p>     -  CAC-40	 489,252  +36.0 pct   -24.9 pct    60,217</p>
<p>     -  Ecu bond	65,300  +45.5 pct    +2.5 pct     7,515</p>
<p>  Financial options  971,864  +20.9 pct   -26.7 pct   482,292</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond  730,070  +47.2 pct   -13.3 pct   247,902</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	  233,020  -23.2 pct   -50.1 pct   225,554</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5542</p>
